file.content:
[
  {
    "id": "c001",
    "name": "Parties",
    "text": "THIS LEASE is entered into as of April 16, 2004 by PATHMARK STORES, INC. , a Delaware corporation, 200 Milik Street, Carteret, New Jersey 07008 (\"Landlord\") and GANDER MOUNTAIN COMPANY, a Minnesota corporation, 4567 American Boulevard West, Minneapolis, Minnesota 55437 (\"Tenant\")."
  },
  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "Recitals — Premises definitions",
    "text": "Landlord owns land described on Exhibit A (“Land”) and located at 528 Harry “L\" Drive, Johnson City, NY 13790. There are located on the Land certain improvements, including a building consisting of approximately forty-seven thousand, four hundred fifty (47,450) square feet (\"Buliding\"). The Building, other improvements and Land, together with all rights, privileges and easements including the parking, entrances, exits, access routes to and from all roads and all related and future improvements, are collectively referred to as the \"Premises.\" The Building and Land are depicted on the site plan attached as Exhibit B."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "1. Premises",
    "text": "1. PREMISES. Landiord hereby leases to Tenant and Tenant hereby leases from Landlord the Premises, upon the terms and conditions set forth in this Lease,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "1.1 Rentable Area",
    "text": "1.1 Rentable Area. “\"Rentable Area\" means the number of square feet of floor area on the main level of the Building, excluding without limitation any basement, mezzanine or balcony, measured and located within the Building from the outside of the exterior walls and the center line of any common (or party) walls."
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "1.2 Rentable Area of the Premises",
    "text": "1.2 Rentable Area of the Premises. “Rentable Area of the Premises\" means fortyseven thousand, four hundred fifty (47,480) square feet (excluding without limitation any basement, mezzanine or balcony). Af any time Landlord or Tenant may, at its cost, have the Rentable Area measured in accordance with the formula set forth in this Lease by an architect reasonably acceptable to Landlord and Tenant. In the event the architect determines that the actual Rentable Area differs from that set forth in this Lease, the parties shall amend all relevant provisions of this Lease (including, without limitation, Base Rent) to accurately reflect the square footage. Changes in the Rentable Area will be in effect on the first day of the month following such change."
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "2. Initial Term",
    "text": "2. INITIAL TERM. The initial term of this Lease shall be fifteen (15) years."
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "2.1 Commencement Date",
    "text": "2.4 Commencement Date. The \"Commencement Date’ shail be the Delivery Date (as such term is defined in Section §.1). The “Rent Commencement Date” shall be the earlier of (a) the date which is four months (4) months after the Commencement Date; or (b) the date Tenant opens the Premises fo the public for retail business operations."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "2.2 Expiration Date",
    "text": "2.2 Expiration Date. Unless extended as provided in this Lease, this Lease shail expire at midnight on the date which is the last day of the fifteenth (15ih) Lease Year, subject to Section 3.3."
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "2.3 Confirmation of Dates",
    "text": "2.3 Confirmation of Dates. Within ten (10} days affer requested by either party, Landlord and Tenant shall confirm in writing the actual Commencement Date, expiration date and option dates by completing the Confirmation of Dates attached hereto as Exhibit C."
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "2.4 Lease Year",
    "text": "2.4 Lease Year. \"Lease Year\" means the twelve (12) month period beginning with the Commencement Date, or the first day of the first full month of the term if the Commencement Date is other than the first day of a month, and each successive twelve-month period thereafter during the term of this Lease."
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "3. Options to Renew",
    "text": "3. OPTIONS TO RENEW. If Tenantis not in default with respect to any ofits obligations under the terms and conditions of this Lease after notice and expiration of any applicable cure period, Tenant shall have the option to renew this Lease for three (3) consecutive renewal terms, each for five (5) Lease Years and each subject to the following terms and conditions:"
  },
  {
    "id": "c012",
    "name": "3.1 Terms",
    "text": "34 Terms. Each renewal term shall be upon the same terms and conditions of this Lease except that the Rent shall be as adjusted sel forth in Section 4,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c013",
    "name": "3.2 Automatic Renewal/Notice of Nonrenewal",
    "text": "3.2 Automatic Renewal/Notice af Nonrenewal, Tenant's options to renew shail be automatically exercised with no action required by Tenant; provided, however, if Tenant elecis not to renew, Tenant must give written notice to Landlord of Tenant's election not to renew atleast one (1) year prior to the expiration of the initial or renewal term then in effect, which notice shall also include, if applicable, Tenant's election nat to extend to January 31 as set forth in Section 3.3."
  },
  {
    "id": "c014",
    "name": "3.3 Automatic Extension to January 31",
    "text": "3.3 Automatic Extension to January 31. Regardless of Tenant's renewal or nonrenewal, Tenant shall have, unless the last day of the Lease term shall be January 31 of any year, the option to extend (or further renew, as the case may be) the term of this Lease for such period of time as shail cause the last day of the term of this Lease fo be the January 31 next succeeding the date upon which the term of this Lease would expire but for the exercise of this option. This option shall be automatically exercised with no action required by Tenant, provided, however, if Tenant elects not to extend to January 31, Tenant must give written notice to Landlord of Tenant's election not to extend until January 31 atleast one (1) year prior to the expiration of the initial or renewal term then in effect."
  },
  {
    "id": "c015",
    "name": "4. Rent",
    "text": "4. RENT. Commencing on the Rent Commencement Date, Tenant agrees io pay to Landiord, at Landlord's notice address in Section 25.8 or at such other place designated in writing by Landiord, rent (\"Rent\") for the Premises consisting of the Base Rent as set forth in Section 4.1, Percentage Rent as set forth in Section 4.2 and Additional Rent as set forth in Section 4.3, in each case without deduction or setoff for any reason whatsoever."
  },
  {
    "id": "c016",
    "name": "4.1 Base Rent",
    "text": "4.1 Base Rent. The Base Rent for the Premises (\"Base Rent”) is based on the Rentable Area of the Premises and is as follows. Base Rent payments shall be made in advance on or before the first business day of each month. Rent for any partial month at the beginning or end of the term of this Lease shall be prorated based upon the actual number of days of such month included in the Lease term. Years Per Square Foot Annual Total Monthly Installment 4-5 $5.50 $260,975.00 $21,748.00 (initial term) 6-10 $6.30 $298,935.00 $24,911.00 (initiat term) 41-75 $7.25 $344,013.00 $28,668.00 (initial term) 16-20 $8.35 $396,208.00 $33,017.00 {first option) 21-25 The Base Rent for the second (2) option period shall be equal to the greater of (a} one hundred fifteen percent (115%) of the Base Rent for the first (1°) aption period (\"First Option Period Base Rent’); or (b} an amount equal to the total of (1) the First Option Period Base Rent, plus (2) an amount equal to ([) the First Option Period Base Rent times {ii} the percentage (expressed as a fraction) by which the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers (the “CPI’} increases between the first day of the first (1\") option period and the last day thereof. {second option) 26-30 The Base Rent for the third (3) option period shall be equal to the greater of (a) one hundred fifteen percent (115%) of the Base Rent for the second (2nd) option period (“Second Option Period Base Rent\"); or (b) an amount equal to the total of (1} the Second Option Period Base Rent, plus (2) an amount equal to (i) the Second Option Period Base Rent times (ii) the percentage (expressed as a fraction) by which the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers (fhe “CP?”) increases between the first day of the second (2\"°) option period and the last day thereof, (third option)"
  },
  {
    "id": "c017",
    "name": "4.1 Non-retail Transfer adjustment",
    "text": "in the event of an assignment or subleasing for a use ather than a retail use such that Percentage Rent would not be applicable (a “Non-retail Transfer), Tenant and Landlord agree that annual Base Rent hereunder shall be increased by an amount obtained by (1) calculating the Percentage Rent owing for each of the prior five (5} Lease Years; (2) selecting the three (3) highest of such five (5) amounts; and (3) calculating the average of such three (3) highest amounts."
  },
  {
    "id": "c018",
    "name": "4.2 Percentage Rent",
    "text": "4.2 Percentage Rent, In addition to the Base Rent provided for in Section 4.1, Tenant agrees to pay percentage rent (\"Percentage Rent\") to Landlord in an amount equal to three percent (3%) of Gross Sales (as such term is defined in this Section) for a particular Lease Year in excess of thirteen million dollars ($13,000,000,00) (“Percentage Rent Threshold\"), provided, however, that in the event of a partial Lease Year at the end of the term hereof or in the event of a Non-retail Transfer, the Percentage Rent Threshold for such partial Lease Year shalt be the total of the Allocated Thresholds (as defined in this Section) for the months within such partial Lease Year (or a prorated Allocated Threshold in any such partial month). For purposes of this Lease, each month of the year shall be allocated a portion of the Percentage Reni Threshold as follows (each, an “Allocated Threshold”); January: $ 65,000.00 February: $ 65,000.00 - March: $ 78,000.00 April: $ 78,000.00 May: $ 91,000.00 June: $104,000.00 July: $ 78,000,00 August: $104,000.00 September: $156,000.00 October: $130,000.00 November: $143,000.00 December: $208,000.00."
  },
  {
    "id": "c019",
    "name": "4.2 Gross Sales definition",
    "text": "The term \"Gross Sales” means the gross amount received by Tenant from all orders taken, placed or filled, and all sales and services made or rendered, and all rental fees, in or from the 3 Premises, whether for cash or credit, provided, however, that Gross Sales shall not include: (a) receipts from vending machines, coin-operated amusement devices and pay telephones; (b) receipts from the sale of gift certificates until such are redeemed on the Premises (provided that any permanent reduction of the value of a gift certificate for non-use, the value of any gift certificate after which Tenant may, under applicable law or the terms of such certificate, cancel for the benefit of Tenant and the value of any gift certificate deemed a “sale” by FASB accounting standards or treated as a sale on Tenant's books and records shall be treated as Gross Sales hereunder); (c} any refund or return which is made fo any customer to the extent the refund is for a sale previously included in Gross Sales (provided that the exclusion of such refund shall not apply to any sale made in a manner which did not result in the inclusion of the original sale in Gross Sales); (d) any sales tax or other payment required by governmental law or regulation; (e) receipts from orders placed at the Premises, but filled elsewhere (provided that such exclusion shall apply only if such receipts are included in a percentage rent calculation at such other location); (f} bad debts and \"nonsufficient funds\" checks (provided that subsequent receipts for collection of same shall be included in Gross Sales); (g) sales of fixtures or equipment and bulk sales of inventory not in the ordinary course of business; (h) any charge paid by Tenant as a finance charge for credit card services; (i) receipts from the sales of hunting, fishing or other ticenses or permits and other receipts which are remitted to a governmental or other licensing entity (provided that any receipts retained by Tenant shall be included in Gross Sales); (j) the exchange or transfer of merchandise between the stores of Tenant, if any, where such exchange or transfers of merchandise is made solely for the convenient operation of the business of Tenant and not for the purpose of consummating a sale made in, from or upon the Premises or for the purpose of depriving Landlord of the benefit of a sale; (k) sales of iterns for charitable purposes; (1) insurance proceeds."
  },
  {
    "id": "c020",
    "name": "4.2 Payment, reporting and audit",
    "text": "Percentage Rent shall be due and payable annually within forty-five (45) days after the end of the applicable Lease Year, Within thirty (30) days after the end of each calendar quarter, Tenant shall deliver a report to Landtord of ifs Gross Sales for the applicable quarter, Said report shalt be certified by a corporate officer responsible for financial reporting for Tenant and prepared in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles, consistently applied. Said report and alt other financial information that Tenant gives to Landlord (including with regard to Tenant's Gross Sales) shall be confidential, and Landtord shail not disclose said report or any other such financial information of Tenant without, in each instance, Tenant's prior written consent. Should Landlord require an audit of Tenant's records of Gross Sales pertaining to the Premises, Tenant agrees to make available to Landlord, at Tenant's corporate offices, all of Tenant's books and records necessary to accomplish said audit. Landlord's right fo audit such records shall be at Landlord's expense and must be exercised within three (3) years after the applicable report of Gross Sales, and such right may be exercised by Landiord only one time in any consecutive twelve (12) month period. In the event that an audit reveals an underpayment of three percent (3%) ar more of Percentage Rent, Tenant shail reimburse Landlord for the cost of the audit,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c021",
    "name": "4.2 No Gross Sales or operating representations",
    "text": "Tenant has made no representations or warranties with respect to the level of Gross Sales from the Premises and expressly disclaims any such representations or warranties, Further, Tenant has made no covenant to continuously operate upon the Premises and Landlord acknowledges that Tenant has no obligation to operate for the Specific Permitted Use (as such term Is defined in Section 8.1) or any other business upon the Premises."
  },
  {
    "id": "c022",
    "name": "4.3 Additional Rent",
    "text": "4.3 Additional Rent. Tenant shall pay as additional rent (“Additional Rent’) all amounts required to be paid by Tenant under the terms of this Lease, including Section 6."
  },
  {
    "id": "c023",
    "name": "4.4 Late Fee",
    "text": "4.4 Late Fee, Tenant hereby acknowledges that the late payment by Tenant to Landlord of Rent, Percentage Rent or any Additional Rent or other sums due hereunder will cause Landlord to incur costs not contemplated in this Lease, the exact amount of which will be extremely difficult and impracticable to ascertain. Such costs include, but are not limited to, processing, 4 administrative and accounting costs. Accordingly, if any installment of Rent, Percentage Rent or any additional rent or any other sum due from Tenant shall not be received by Landlord within ten (10) days after such amount shall be due, Tenant shall pay fo Landlord a late charge equal to five (5%) percent of such overdue amount as liquidated damages. The parties hereby agree that such late charges represent a fair and reasonable estimate of the costs Landlord will incur by reason of late payment by Tenant. Acceptance of such late charge by Landlord shall in no event constitute a waiver of Tenant's default with respect to such overdue amount, nor prevent Landlord fram exercising any of the other rights and remedies granted under this Lease. It is understoad and agreed between the parties that, although there is a ten (10} day grace period with respect to the implementation of tate charges pursuant to this Section, Section 17 is controlting with respect to the time periods required for payment of Rent, Percentage Rent and all items of Additional Rent hereunder, and in the event that Tenant does not pay any such Rent or other amounts within the time periods set forth in Section 17 hereunder, notwithstanding that no late charge may have accrued under this Section, the terms of Section 17 with respect to default hereunder shall apply."
  },
  {
    "id": "c024",
    "name": "4.4 Returned-check charge",
    "text": "Any check remitted to Landlord that fails to \"clear\" In the banking process for any reason whatsoever, unless caused by Landlord, will cause a thirty-five dollar ($35.00) service charge to be added to Tenant's account as Additional Rent."
  },
  {
    "id": "c025",
    "name": "4.5 Tenant Improvement Allowance; Base Rent Credit",
    "text": "4,5 Tenant Improvement Alowance: Base Rent Credit. Tenant shall be entitled to a credit against the Base Rent in the amount of the lesser of (a) six hundred seventy-five thousand dollars ($675,000.00); or (b) the amount actually expended by Tenantin the construction of Tenant's Work in either case, (\"Base Rent Credit”), as follows: in each Lease Year (until the Base Rent Credit is applied in full}, Tenant shall be entitled to a monthly credit of eight thousand, fifty dollars ($8,050.00) (“Monthly Credit”). Within thirty (30) days following the Rent Commencement Date (and, if such amount expended has not yet exceeded six hundred seventy-five thousand daliars {$675,000.00}, within thirty (30) days follawing the completion of Tenant's Work), the chief financial officer of Tenant shall certify the amount actually expended by Tenant for Tenant's Work."
  },
  {
    "id": "c026",
    "name": "5.1 Condition on Delivery",
    "text": "5.1 Condition on Delivery. Landlord agrees to deliver possession of the Premises to Tenant upon the execution and delivery of this lease by Landlord and Tenant and upon delivery of required insurance evidence by Tenant. The date of delivery shall be referred to herein as the “Delivery Date.” Landlord and Tenant agree to confirm the Delivery Date in writing. Tenant shall accept the Building in its “as is” condition, with all faults and defects, on the Delivery Date, without representation or warranty."
  },
  {
    "id": "c027",
    "name": "5.2 Tenant's Work",
    "text": "5.2 Tenant's Work. Tenant may, atifs own cost and expense, equip and build out the Premises as Tenant deems necessary to operate its business (\"Tenant's Work\") in a manner consistent with a Gander Mountain prototype building. Tenant's Work shall be deemed Improvements under Section 14 of this Lease. Tenant agrees fo submit plans and specifications for Tenant's Work (“Tenant's Work Plans”) to Landlord. Landlord shall only have the right to approve, which approval shail not be unreasonably conditioned, withheld or delayed and which shail be deemed given if Landlord has not objected thereto within fifteen (15) days of such submission, any component of the Tenant's Work Plans which adversely affects the structural integrity of the Building. if Landtord does object thereto, Tenant shall be given fifteen (15) days in which to address such objection and resubmit revised Tenant's Work Plans to Landlord, whose approval shail be deemed given if Landlord has not objected thereto within fifteen (15) days of such submission. If Landlord still objects thereto, Tenant may terminate this Lease within fifteen (15) days following such objection."
  },
  {
    "id": "c028",
    "name": "5.3 Utilities",
    "text": "9.3 Utilities. Tenant shall pay all charges for gas, electricity, water, sewer, heat or other fuel or power or any other utility or service used on the Premises on or after the Delivery Dale 5 and during this Lease, All utilities to the Premises will be separately metered and the branch utility lines serving the Premises will not serve any other property,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c029",
    "name": "5.4 Exterior Signs",
    "text": "5.4 Exterior Signs. Tenant shail have the right to erect Tenant's storefront and exterior storefront signs to identify Tenant's business on the Premises and shall have exclusive use of the pyion sign on the Land (as may be identified on Exhibit B), in each case in a manner consistent with a Gander Mountain prototype sign package from time to time. Tenant may change its signs, at its cost, af any time during this Lease. Any sign installed must comply with all laws, ordinances, rules and regulations of any governmental authority, including any permitting requirements. Landlord shall not permit any other signs, billboards or posters to be displayed on any portion of the Building, the pylon or the Land, other than with the prior written approval of Tenant, which approval Tenant may withhold in its sole and absolute discretion. All signs shall be removed at the expiration or earlier termination of this Lease."
  },
  {
    "id": "c030",
    "name": "5.5 Dish Antenna",
    "text": "5.5 Dish Antenna. Landlord grants Tenant the right to install a dish antenna and/or other communications equipment on the roof of the Building at a location acceptable to Landlord and Tenant. Tenant shall be responsible for the repair and maintenance of any such equipment during the term of this Lease."
  },
  {
    "id": "c031",
    "name": "6.1 Definition of Taxes",
    "text": "6.4 Definition. \"Tax(es}” means all real estate taxes and assessments from time to time jevied or assessed against the Land (including without limitation against buildings, structures, lands, equipment and improvements therein) by municipal or other governmental authorities having jurisdiction together with all reasonable costs and expenses (including legal and other professional fees) incurred by the Landlord in good faith in contesting or appealing any such real estate taxes and assessments and all real estate taxes and assessments which may at any time be imposed in lieu of, in addition to or in substitution of same,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c032",
    "name": "6.2.1 Taxes",
    "text": "6.2.1 Taxes. Except as may be otherwise provided herein, commencing on the Rent Commencement Date, Tenant agrees to pay, as Additional Rent, Taxes which are due and payable on or after the Rent Commencement Date and during the Lease term {regardless of whether such Taxes are attributable to or on account of a prior year). Taxes for the initial and final years of the term shall be prorated on a per diem basis with Tenant only responsible for its portion of Taxes allocable to the Lease term. The parties’ obligations hereunder to prorate the last year’s Taxes shall survive the termination of this Lease."
  },
  {
    "id": "c033",
    "name": "6.2.2 Billing",
    "text": "6.2.2 Billing. Upon receipt of each tax bill from the taxing authority, Landlord shall furnish Tenant with a copy. A copy of a tax bill or assessment bill submitted by Landlord to Tenant shall at all times be conclusive evidence of the amount of Taxes assessed or fevied against the property to which such bill relates. Tenant shall have no abligation to make monthly escrow deposits for Taxes unless required by a fee mortgagee. Tenant shall pay to Landlord such Taxes at least fifteen (15) days prior to Landlord's due date; provided, however, that in the event that Landlord does not provide the applicable tax bill before at least twenty-one (21) days prior to Landlord’s due date, then Tenant shail not have to pay to Landlord such Taxes until five (5) days after receipt of such bill. Landlord agrees to timely pay all Taxes before the same become delinquent and to promptly forward to Tenant a copy of the \"paid\" tax bill or other proof of payment reasonably satisfactory to Tenant,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c034",
    "name": "6.2.3 Installments",
    "text": "6.2.3 Installments. If bylaw, any such Tax Is payable or may at the option of the taxpayer be paid in installments (whether or not interest shail accrue on the unpaid balance of such Tax), Landlord shall pay the same (and any accrued interest on the unpaid balance of such Tax) in installments as the same respectively become due and only those installments coming due within the applicable year shail be included in Taxes for that year. Any Tax relating to a fiscal period of the taxing authority, a part of which period is included within the Lease term (after the Rent Commencement Date) and a part of which is included in a period of time before the Rent Commencement Date or after the Lease term, shall be adjusted so that Taxes shall only include that proportion of such Tax which falls after the Reni Commencement Date and within the Lease term. With respect to any Tax for public improvements or benefits which by law is payable, or at the option of the taxpayer may be paid in installments, Taxes shall include only those installments which become due and payable during the Lease term."
  },
  {
    "id": "c035",
    "name": "6.3 Tenant Not to Pay Certain Taxes",
    "text": "6.3 Tenant Not to Pay Certain Taxes. Nothing in this Lease shall require Tenant to pay any giff, franchise, estate, inheritance, succession, capital levy or transfer tax of Landlord, or any income, excess profits, or revenue tax or any other tax, assessment, charge or levy upon the Rent payable by Tenant under this Lease, and all such taxes shall be paid or discharged by Landlord. Notwithstanding the foregaing, Tenant shall pay any tax assessment, charge or impost, which is a specific substitute in whole or in part for Taxes whether such tax, assessment, charge or impost is based upon real estate, gross receipts from real estate, transfer of real estate or any other source of determination or measurement; provided, however, that if fhe amount or rate of any such tax so levied against the income of Landlord as a specific substitute in whote or in part for such Taxes shall be increased by reason of any other income, receipts or property owned by Landlord, then and in that event, Tenant shall not be obligated to pay such increased amount, but only such tax as Landlord would be obligated {o pay in case it derived no income from any source other than the Premises nor owned any property other than the Premises."
  },
  {
    "id": "c036",
    "name": "6.4 Right to Contest Taxes",
    "text": "6.4 Right to Contest Taxes. Tenant shall have the right to request that the Landlord contest the amount or validity of any Tax upon the Premises and the right to inifiate such contest directly (whereupon Landlord shall cooperate with Tenant at Tenant's expense), in each case by appropriate legal proceedings and at Tenant's cost and expense. If any such contest results in a refund of Taxes, Tenant shall be entitled to any refund of any Tax and penalties or interest thereon. if any such contest results in additional Taxes, Tenant shall pay such Taxes if such contest was initiated by Landlord solely at Tenant's request or initiated by Tenant independently."
  },
  {
    "id": "c037",
    "name": "6.5.1 Real Estate Taxes",
    "text": "6.5.1 Real Estate Taxes. All real estate taxes assessed and due with respect to the Land and nat delinquent have been paid; and"
  },
  {
    "id": "c038",
    "name": "6.5.2 Assessments",
    "text": "6.5.2 Assessments. To Landiord’s knowledge, without any independent investigation, there are no assessments of any kind, levied or assessed against the Land (including without limitation any assessments incurred or levied as a result of Landlord’s initial construction or development of the Land or any portion thereof or the Premises)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c039",
    "name": "6.6 Taxes on Leasehold",
    "text": "6.6 Taxes on Leasehold. Tenant shall pay before delinquency all state, county and municipal taxes assessed during the term against Tenant's leasehold interest and personal property of any kind, owned by or placed in, upon or about the Premises by Tenant. In addition, Tenant shall pay any and all taxes assessed or levied against Tenant as sales or use taxes on any and all of the rentals paid by Tenant under this Lease (“Sales or Use Taxes\"). If Landlord is required, pursuant to applicable law, to collect from Tenant any Sales or Use Taxes on behalf of any applicable f governmental authorities, Tenant shail pay those to Landlord within thirty (30) days of its receipt of the bill and statement from Landlord."
  },
  {
    "id": "c040",
    "name": "7. Net Lease",
    "text": "7. NET LEASE. After the Rent Commencement Date, Tenant shall have no right to cancel this Lease, seek a diminution of Rent, sue for damages, or assert any other contractual, legal or equitable remedy based either on (a) a claim that Landlord failed to deliver possession in accordance with the terms of this Lease; or (b) a claim that the size, location, layout, dimensions or construction of the Building, service areas (if any), sidewalks, parking or other common areas {if any), or any other facilities to be furnished by Landlord, were not completed or furnished in accordance with the terms of this Lease. Tenant understands, acknowledges and agrees that the Rent (including Base Rent, Percentage Rent and Additional Rent) reserved to Landiard in this Lease is net of all expenses, and that Landlord shail not be required to perform any work for or provide any services to Tenant or the Premises, except as may be specifically set out herein. Notwithstanding the foregoing, if during the term hereof Landlord is in default under any of its Lease obligations, Tenant shall have such rights al aw or equity to which it may be entitled, except that Tenant hereby waives any right to cancel or terminate this Lease or seek a diminution of Rent unless such right is explicitly reserved to Tenant under the terms of this Lease. Upon the Rent Commencement Date, Tenant shall be deemed ta have certified to Landford and the holder of any mortgage to which this Lease is, or shall thereafter be, subject and subordinate, that the Premises have been delivered fo it in accordance with the terms of this Lease and that possession thereof has been fully and completely accepted by Tenant who is then in possession of same, and that the term of this Lease and the opening for business to the public and the date for the payment of Rent hereunder have all theretofore commenced and that the Premises, the parking area, and all other portions of fhe Premises have been completed in accordance with the requirements and terms of this Lease and that there is not any offset of any Rent nor any violation of any of the Lease terms on the part of Landiord, except as may be specifically set out herein, in each case as of the Rent Commencement Date. The foregoing provisions shall be self-operative and no further instrument, letter or certificate shall be required by Landlord or any such mortgagee unless either said Landlord or mortgagee shall deem same appropriate in which event, in confirmation of the foregoing, Tenant shall, without cost to Landlord promptly execute, in writing, any instrument, letter and/or certificate containing the foregoing and such other like provisions in regard to the condition of the Premises, the Building, the Premises {and/or any portions thereof); the Rent, ferm and date of the opening of the Premises for business to the public as shall be requested by Landlord and/or said rnortgagee."
  },
  {
    "id": "c041",
    "name": "8.1 Use",
