 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c032", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The first sentence makes Tenant pay Taxes falling due in the term \"regardless of whether such Taxes are attributable to or on account of a prior year,\" while the next sentence limits Tenant to \"its portion of Taxes allocable to the Lease term.\" The provision thus contradicts itself on pre-term tax years.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c033", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Making a tax bill \"at all times ... conclusive evidence of the amount of Taxes\" is hard to square with Section 6.4, which gives Tenant the right to contest the amount or validity of any Tax. A court could be asked whether the conclusive-evidence clause forecloses Tenant's contest rights.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.17}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c034", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The proration rule that Taxes include only the proportion falling within the Lease term after the Rent Commencement Date cannot be squared with Section 6.2.1's \"regardless of whether such Taxes are attributable to or on account of a prior year.\" Which rule applies to a straddling fiscal year is left open.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c035", "issues": [
