 {"clause_id": "c027", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"[I]n a manner consistent with a Gander Mountain prototype building\" is an external, undefined and changeable standard against which Tenant's Work must be judged. The section also gives Landlord approval rights only over components \"which adversely affect[] the structural integrity of the Building,\" a phrase with no stated threshold.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c028", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c029", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Tenant's exclusive right to \"the pylon sign on the Land (as may be identified on Exhibit B)\" depends on an Exhibit B site plan that is not completed in the instrument, which merely lists items \"[t]o Show.\" A court would have to determine which pylon, if any, the grant reaches.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c030", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Installation is permitted only \"at a location acceptable to Landlord and Tenant,\" an agreement to agree with no default location and no standard of reasonableness stated in the section. Section 25.12's general reasonableness rule applies only where consent is \"required,\" which may not cover mutual acceptability.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.14}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c031", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The definition sweeps Landlord's contest costs into \"Tax(es)\" payable by Tenant, while Section 6.4 puts contests at Tenant's cost and gives Tenant the refunds. A court could be asked whether Tenant pays Landlord's contest expenses on top of the costs Section 6.4 already assigns to it.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c032", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The first sentence makes Tenant pay Taxes falling due in the term \"regardless of whether such Taxes are attributable to or on account of a prior year,\" while the next sentence limits Tenant to \"its portion of Taxes allocable to the Lease term.\" The provision thus contradicts itself on pre-term tax years.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c033", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Making a tax bill \"at all times ... conclusive evidence of the amount of Taxes\" is hard to square with Section 6.4, which gives Tenant the right to contest the amount or validity of any Tax. A court could be asked whether the conclusive-evidence clause forecloses Tenant's contest rights.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.17}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c034", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The proration rule that Taxes include only the proportion falling within the Lease term after the Rent Commencement Date cannot be squared with Section 6.2.1's \"regardless of whether such Taxes are attributable to or on account of a prior year.\" Which rule applies to a straddling fiscal year is left open.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c035", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"[A]ny other tax, assessment, charge or levy upon the Rent\" is a general catch-all following a list of Landlord-specific transfer and income taxes, and it collides with the following sentence's substitute-tax obligation measured by \"gross receipts from real estate.\" Which sentence captures a gross-receipts or rent tax is contestable.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c036", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The last sentence — Tenant pays additional Taxes if the contest \"was initiated by Landlord solely at Tenant's request or initiated by Tenant independently\" — leaves unaddressed who bears additional Taxes from a contest Landlord initiates on its own. \"[R]equest that the Landlord contest\" also imposes no stated duty on Landlord to do so.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c037", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The warranty that taxes \"assessed and due ... and not delinquent have been paid\" is self-cancelling as drafted: taxes that have been paid are neither due nor delinquent. What it warrants about unpaid but not-yet-delinquent taxes is unclear.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.12}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c038", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c039", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Requiring Tenant to pay sales or use taxes \"on any and all of the rentals paid by Tenant\" is difficult to reconcile with Section 6.3, which bars requiring Tenant to pay \"any other tax, assessment, charge or levy upon the Rent payable by Tenant.\" A court could be asked which section governs a rent tax.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c040", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The waiver of any right to cancel, seek diminution of Rent or sue for damages sits against Section 17.2, which expressly lets Tenant cure, offset costs and abate Base, Percentage and Additional Rent on Landlord's default, and against the termination rights in Sections 15.4, 16.2 and 26. A court would have to decide how far the \"unless such right is explicitly reserved\" carve-out reaches.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c041", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The grant of \"any lawful purpose, including without limitation\" a long enumerated list, followed by a list of prohibited purposes, sets a general permission against enumerated specifics and invites an ejusdem generis or expressio unius reading of the permitted scope. Whether a use outside both lists is permitted, and what \"other uses incidental thereto\" covers, is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28},
   {"issue": "The prohibition on use as \"a shooting gallery\" is hard to square with Section 23.3, in which Landlord acknowledges Tenant's contemplated \"display, sale and demonstration of firearms, smokeless powder, black powder, ammunition.\" A court could be asked whether an indoor range or firearms demonstration area falls within the prohibition.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c042", "issues": [
   {"issue": "A section titled \"No Operating Covenant\" opens with an affirmative covenant that Tenant \"shall open a Gander Mountain store on the Premises within one (1) year after the Delivery Date,\" and then says no provision imposes obligations respecting operation of the Premises. The duration and enforceability of the opening obligation is left in doubt.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c043", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Landlord's recapture notice \"must be exercised, if at all, by providing Tenant with written notice following the expiration of such nine (9) month period,\" fixing no outside deadline, so the right is open-ended in time. Whether \"cease for a period in excess of nine (9) consecutive months\" is measured net of the listed excluded causes is also unstated.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c044", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c045", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Permission to use \"any portion of the Premises and the Land\" for outside display and storage is unbounded and open-ended (\"may include, but are not limited to\"), with no limit protecting the parking supply the Lease elsewhere measures by ratio in Sections 16.2 and 26.5. How much of the Land may be given over to storage is not stated.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.14}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c046", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The restriction bites only \"to the extent that such sales, in the aggregate, exceed five percent (5%) of its retail sales,\" leaving \"its\" ungrounded — the transferee's sales at that property, or company-wide — and giving no measurement period. The trailing clause \"and no party has been granted any exclusive use with regard to the Specific Permitted Use\" is grammatically detached from the operative prohibition.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.50},
   {"issue": "The covenant runs only \"[f]or so long as the Premises are used for the Specific Excluded Use,\" yet Section 8.2 lets Tenant cease operations entirely in its sole discretion and Section 8.1 permits any lawful use. A court could be asked whether the radius restriction lapses whenever Tenant stops the outdoor-retail use.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.35}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c047", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The remedy clause gives damages and injunctive relief without the stipulation, made in Section 3 of the Exhibit D Declaration of Restrictions, that damages are inadequate. A court could be asked whether the availability of damages under this section defeats injunctive relief for the same breach.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c048", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Tenant shall remain fully liable on this Lease\" after any transfer is not squared with clause (b)(2), which permits transfer to an entity that \"succeeds to the business of Tenant\" by merger or asset sale, where the transferor may cease to exist. Whether any assignment can release Tenant is left unstated.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c049", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The carve-out relieving Tenant of replacing the parking lot, roof or major building systems in the last three years of the term leaves no one obliged to replace them, since Section 7 provides Landlord need perform no work except as specifically set out. A court could be asked who bears a required roof replacement in that window.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c050", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The self-insurance proviso — \"provided such self-insurance may not exceed five hundred thousand dollars ($500,000.00)\" — has an unclosed parenthesis and does not say whether the cap is per occurrence, per year or in the aggregate. The five-year adjustment to \"a CPI index or other benchmark in customary use in the insurance industry\" likewise names no determinate standard.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
 ]}
]}

