{
  "id": "c075",
  "name": "18.3 Landlord's Sale of Premises",
  "text": "18.3 Landlord's Sale of Premises. Landlord shall have the right at any time to sell or transfer its interest in the Land or Premises to any person, firm or corporation whatsoever; provided, however, that any such sale or transfer shail be subject to this Lease and that all of Landford's covenants and obligations contained herein shall be binding upon the subsequent owner or owners thereof and that such transferee from Landlord shall in writing assume the obligations of Landlord hereunder; further, provided, however, Landiord shall remain fully tiable on this Lease for any claims or other matiers arising out of the default, negligence or action of Landlord prior to such transfer. if Tenant executes an estoppel certificate in connection with a transfer of Landlord's interest herein, Landlord's ilabllity following the transfer of its interest herein shall be limited fo those matters set out by Tenant in such estoppel certificate."
},
{
  "id": "c076",
  "name": "18.3 Landlord definition and liability limitation",
  "text": "The term “Landlord” as used in this Lease means only the owner from time to time of the Premises or the owner from time to time of a leasehold interest in the Land (if Landiord's interest is that of a lessee under a ground lease), so that in the event of the sale of the Premises (or leasehold interest) or an assignment of this Lease, or a new demise of the Premises (and/or leasehold), Landlord named herein, and any successor thereto other than the then owner (or then ground lessee, as appropriate ) shall be and hereby is entirely freed and relieved of all obligations of Landiord hereunder subsequently accruing. His specifically understood and agreed that each successor landiord hereunder shall be deemed to have expressly assumed ail obligations hereunder of its predecessors with respect to this Lease. There shall be no personal (or entity) liability of Landlord (nor Landlord's agents, if any) in respect of any of the covenants, conditions or provisions of this Lease. in the event of a breach or default by Landlord of any of its obligations under this Lease beyond the applicable grace and/or cure period, or if Landlord shall otherwise be liable to Tenant for any reason whatsoever Tenant shail look solely to the interest, if any, of the applicable Landtord-in the Premises for the satisfaction of Tenant's remedies."
},
{
  "id": "c077",
  "name": "18.4 Tenant Financing",
  "text": "18.4 TenantFinancing. Tenant shail have the absolute right from time to time during the term hereof and without Landlord's further approval, written or otherwise, to collaterally assign or to grant and assign a mortgage or other security interest in Tenant's interest in this Lease and all of Tenant's property to Tenant's lenders in connection with Tenant's financing arrangements. Landiord agrees to execute such confirmation, certificates and other documents (except amendmenis to this Lease unless Landlord hereafter consents) as Tenant's lenders may reasonably request and in a form acceptable to Landlord and Landlord's counsel in connection with any such financing. Landlord may condition its acceptance thereof on the conditions that the applicable secured party unconditionally agree to restore the Premises to the condition required by this Lease on the removal of the secured property, and that the payment of Rent and Additional Rent, including any arrears, until lhe last day of the month in which the secured party is in possession of Tenant's property in the Premises be set forth."
},
{
  "id": "c078",
  "name": "19.1 Authority",
  "text": "19.1 Authority. Landlord has full right and lawful authority to enter into and perform Landlord's obligations under this Lease for the initial term and all renewal terms."
},
{
  "id": "c079",
  "name": "19.2 Fee Owner",
  "text": "19.2 Fee Owner. Landlord is the fee owner of the Land."
},
{
  "id": "c080",
  "name": "19.3 Encumbrances",
  "text": "49.3 Encumbrances. As ofthe Commencement Date, there are no mortgages, security interests or ground leases, or any contracts, leases, tenancies, agreements, restrictions as to use or exclusives entered into by Landlord, affecting or recorded against all or any part of the Land or the Premises, except for the matters specifically set forth in Exhibit G hereto."
},
{
  "id": "c081",
  "name": "19.4 Use",
  "text": "19.4 Use. To the knowledge of Landlord, after securing all necessary governmental permits and approvals the Premises can be used by Tenant for the Specific Permitted Use."
},
{
  "id": "c082",
  "name": "19.5 Survival",
  "text": "49.5 Survival. The foregoing representations and warranties shall survive the expiration or earlier termination of this Lease."
},
{
  "id": "c083",
  "name": "20.1 Authority",
  "text": "20.1 Authority. Tenant is authorized to do business in the state in which the Premises are located."
},
{
  "id": "c084",
  "name": "20.2 Corporate Action",
  "text": "20.2 Corporate Action. Tenant has taken all corporate action necessary to permit its performance under this Lease."
},
{
  "id": "c085",
  "name": "20.3 Valid",
  "text": "20.3 Valid. This Lease is valid and binding upon Tenant."
},
{
  "id": "c086",
  "name": "20.4 Survival",
  "text": "20.4 Survival. The foregoing representations and warranties shall survive the expiration or earlier termination of this Lease."
},
{
  "id": "c087",
  "name": "21. Covenant of Quiet Possession",
  "text": "21. COVENANT OF QUIET POSSESSION. Landlord covenants that subject to the performance by Tenant of the terms and conditions of this Lease, Tenant shall peaceably have and enjoy, during ihe term hereof, the quiet and undisturbed possession of the Premises and ail other rights of Tenant under this Lease for the term of this Lease without interference or interruption by Landlord or any other person or persons lawfully or equitably claiming title by, through or under the Landiord."
},
{
  "id": "c088",
  "name": "22. Surrender of Premises",
  "text": "22, SURRENDER OF PREMISES. Upon expiration of the Lease term, or any earlier termination of this Lease, Tenant shall surrender the Premises, including Improvements made by Tenant (but excluding Tenant's personal property and trade fixtures), to Landlord in good condition and repair, except for ordinary wear and tear, repairs which are Landlord's responsibility pursuant fo its indemnification obligations under Section 13, casualty damage (if it is Landlord's obligation under this Lease to repair such casualty damage) or casualty damage and damage resulting from eminent domain which entitles Tenant to terminate this Lease pursuant to express provisions in this Lease. Tenant shall remove ifs trade fixtures and personal property prior to such surrender, If Tenant does not remove its trade fixtures and personal property prior to such surrender, Landlord may remove and dispose of the same for the account of and at the expense af Tenant."
},
{
  "id": "c089",
  "name": "23.1.1 Environmental Laws",
  "text": "23.1.1 Environmental Laws. \"Environmental Laws\" means all federal, state and locallaws, including statutes, regulations, ordinances, codes, rules and other governmental restrictions and requirements relating fo the discharge of air poflutants, water pollutants or process waste water or otherwise relating fo the environment or solid, liquid or hazardous substances, materials or wastes, including, but not limited to, the Federal Solid Waste Disposal Act, the Federal Clean Air Act, the Federal Clean Water Act, the Federal Resource Conservation and Recovery Act of 1976, the Federal Comprehensive Environmental Responsibility Cleanup and Liability Act of 1980, the Superfund Amendments and Reauthorization Act of 1986, regulations of the Environmental Protection Agency, regulations of the Nuclear Regulatory Agency and regulations of any state department of natural resources or any other state environmental protection agency now or at any time hereafter in effect."
},
{
  "id": "c090",
  "name": "23.1.2 Hazardous Material",
  "text": "23.1.2 Hazardous Material, “Hazardous Materia!\" means any substance, material or waste which is or af any time hereafter becomes regulated as \"hazardous,\" “toxic” or under any other similar designation by any local, state or federal governmental authority. Such terms includes, without fimitation, [a] asbestos, [b] any material, substance or waste defined as a “hazardous waste” pursuant to section 1004 of the Resource Conservation and Recovery Act (42 U.S.C. § 6901, ef seq.), [c] any material, substance or waste defined as a “hazardous substance” pursuant to Section 101 of the Comprehensive Environmental Response, Compensation and Liability Act (42 U.S.C. § 9601, et seq.), [d] any material, substance or waste defined as a \"regulated substance” pursuant to Subchapter IX of the 18 Solid Waste Disposal Act (42 U.S.C. § 6991, et seq.), or fe] petroleum and petroleum products."
},
{
  "id": "c091",
  "name": "23.1.3 Tenant Indemnified Person",
  "text": "23.1.3 Tenant Indemnified Person. \"Tenant indemnified Person* means Tenant and any director, officer, employee, contractor or agent of Tenant."
},
{
  "id": "c092",
  "name": "23.1.4 Landlord Indemnified Person",
  "text": "23.4.4 Landlord indemnified Person. \"Landiord Indemnified Person” means the Landlord and any director, officer, employee, contractor or agent of Landlord."
},
{
  "id": "c093",
  "name": "23.2 Landlord Representations and Warranties",
  "text": "23.2 Landlord Representations and Warranties. Landiord represents to Tenant that it has heretofore provided to Tenant full, accurate and complete copies of any and all reports, studies, and other information in its possession relating to the issue of the presence or suspected presence of any Hazardous Material in, on or about the Premises. Landlord represents and warrants to Tenant that, to Landiord's knowledge and belief without any independent inquiry or investigation: any handling, transportation, storage, treatment or usage of Hazardous Material that has heretofore occurred in, on or about the Premises has been in compliance with ail Environmental Laws: it has no knowledge that any leak, spill, release, discharge, emission or disposal of any Hazardous Materials has occurred in, on or about the Premises except in compliance with all Environmental Laws; to its knowledge, without any independent inquiry or investigation, the Premises {including the Building) is free of any Hazardous Material (including asbestos); and there are no underground storage tanks located in, on or about the Premises."
},
{
  "id": "c094",
  "name": "23.3 Landlord covenant",
  "text": "23.3 Mutual Covenants. Landlord covenants and agrees that no Landlord indemnified Person shall use, generate, place, store, release, or otherwise dispose of, nor permit the use, generation, placing, storage, release or disposal of any Hazardous Material in, on or about the Premises except in strict accordance with ail Environmental Laws, whether in connection with the construction of the Premises or otherwise."
},
{
  "id": "c095",
  "name": "23.3 Tenant covenant",
  "text": "Tenant covenants and agrees that no Tenant indemnified Person shall use, nor permit or suffer the use of, generate, place, store, release, or otherwise dispose of any Hazardous Material in, on or about the Premises except in strict accordance with all Environmental Laws. Without limitation of the foregoing, Landlord acknowledges and agrees that (a) the use of the Premises contemplated by Tenant involves the display, sale and demonstration of firearms, smokeless powder, black powder, ammunition and related materials, as well as camping fuel and other flammable, and certain petroleum products, and (b) such display, sale and demonstration does not violate any of the provisions of this Section to the extent Tenant conducts such display, sale and demonstration in strict accordance with ail Environmental Laws and other federal, state and local laws, rules, orders and regulations which are now existing or hereinafter enacted with respect to the Land and Premises."
},
{
  "id": "c096",
  "name": "23.4 Landlord Indemnity",
  "text": "23.4 Landlord Indemnity. Landlord agrees to indemnify, defend and hold each Tenant Indemnified Person harmless from any and ail loss, cost, damage and expense that arises during or after the Lease term as a result of the inaccuracy or breach of any of the representations, warranties or covenants by Landlord contained in this Section 23. The costs covered by the Landlord’s Indemnification include, without limitation, costs incurred in the investigation of site conditions, reasonable attomeys' fees, engineers and other consultants, costs and expenses incurred by Tenant in exercising any of its rights hereunder and any damages suffered as a result of any termination of this Lease in accordance with this Section 23. Landlord has the right to ‘ provide the defense or, at Landlord's option upon request from Tenant, permit Tenant to conduct its own defense at Landlord's expense. Excluded from the Landlord's indemnification shall be any loss, cost, damage or expense resulting from the presence of any Hazardous Material introduced onto the Premises by any Tenant Indemnified Person, or placed inside fhe four walls of the Building or on, in or under the Premises by an invitee or customer of Tenant during the term of this Lease. This indemnity shall survive the expiration or earfler termination of this Lease."
},
{
  "id": "c097",
  "name": "23.5 Tenant Indemnity",
  "text": "23.5 Tenant indemnity. Tenant hereby agrees to indemnify, defend and hold each Landlord indemnified Person harmless from any and all loss, cost, damage and expense that arises during ar after the Lease term as a result of the introduction onto the Premises of any Hazardous Material by a Tenant Indemnified Person, or any invitee or customer of Tenant, or any breach by Tenant of any covenant contained in this Section 23. The costs covered by Tenant's indemnification include, without limitation, costs incurred in the investigation of site conditions, reasonable fees of attorneys, engineers and other consultants and costs and expenses incurred by Landlord exercising any of its rights hereunder. Tenant has the right to provide the defense or, at Tenant's option upon request from Landlord, permit Landlord to conduct its own defense at Tenant's expense. This indemnity shall survive the expiration or earlier termination of this Lease."
},
{
  "id": "c098",
  "name": "23.6 Remedial Action",
  "text": "23.6 Remedial Action, Landlord and Tenant agree to promptly notify the other in the event such party becomes aware of the presence of any Hazardous Material other than any Hazardous Material which Tenant sells in the ordinary course of business, such as black powder, or any underground storage tank in, on or about the Premises. If any Landlord indemnified Person contaminates the Premises with any Hazardous Material, Landlord shall, at ifs sole cost, promptly commence and diligently pursue actions to clean up and/or remediate such Hazardous Material in accordance with all relevant Environmentat Laws. If any Tenant indemnified Person, or any invitee or customer of Tenant, contaminates the Premises with any Hazardous Material, Tenant shall, at its sole cost and expense and after Landlord approval, promptly commence and diligently pursue actions {o clean up and/or remediate such Hazardous Material in accordance with all relevant Environmental Laws. lf any person or entity other than a Landlord Indemnified Person or a Tenant Indemnified Person, or any invitee or customer of Tenant, contaminates the Premises with any Hazardous Material, Landlord shall, if required by any governmental agency or if the presence of the contamination materially interferes with Tenant's use of the Premises, clean up and/or remediate such contamination in accordance with all relevant Environmental Laws. Any clean up or rededication of the Premises shail be done in such a manner as to minimize any interference with Tenant's use of the Premises."
},
{
  "id": "c099",
  "name": "24.1 Landlord's Compliance",
  "text": "24.1 ‘Landlord's Compliance. The Premises are in compliance with all federal, state and local laws, rules, orders and regulations which are now existing with respect to the Land and Premises as of the Commencement Date, provided that Landlord makes no representation with respect to the compliance of the Premises with the Americans with Disabilities Act."
},
{
  "id": "c100",
  "name": "24.2 Tenant's Compliance",
  "text": "24.2 Tenant's Compliance. Tenant shall observe and comply with all federal, stale and local laws, rules, orders and regulations which are now existing or hereinafter enacted with respect to the Premises, including but not limited to the making of nonstructural alterations, insofar as they are due to Tenant's occupancy; provided, however, in | t such laws, rules, orders and regulations shall require structural changes; ind ubnot fo, the erection of a fire escape or exit, the same shall be complied with by L ole cost, unless such structural changes are required as a result of Tenant's Work, in which event, Tenant shail pay the costs. Tenant shall cause all construction work ta be done in a workmantike manner and in compliance with ail applicable faws, ordinances, rules, regulations and all lawful requirements of the nationat fire protection code. At no expense to Landiord, Landlord will cooperate with Tenant to obtain any needed permit, license, approval or authorization."
},
{
  "id": "c101",
  "name": "25.1 Headings",
  "text": "25.1 Headings. The titles fo sections of this Lease are solely for convenience of reference and shall not in any way limit or amplify the terms."
},
{
  "id": "c102",
  "name": "25.2 Successors and Assigns",
  "text": "252 Successors and Assigns. All of the terms and conditions contained in this Lease shall Inure to and be binding upon Landlord and Tenant and their respective heirs, executors, administrators, successors and assigns."
},
{
  "id": "c103",
  "name": "25.3 Exhibits",
  "text": "25.3 Exhibits. In the event of any conflicts between the terms of this Lease and any exhibit, the terms of this Lease will prevail."
},
{
  "id": "c104",
  "name": "25.4 Access to Premises",
  "text": "25.4 Access to Premises. Upon reasonable prior notice, but in no event less than twenty-four (24) hours (except in the case of an emergency), Landlord may enter the Premises during Tenant's business hours for purposes of inspection, to show the Premises to prospective purchasers and lenders, or to perform maintenance and repair obligations imposed upon Landiord by this Lease. Landlord agrees not to unreasonably interfere with Tenant's business by such entry."
},
{
  "id": "c105",
  "name": "25.5 Entire Agreement",
  "text": "25.5 Entire Agreement. This Lease contains all covenants and agreements between Landlord and Tenant. No prior agreements or understandings pertaining thereto shall be valid or of any force or effect and the covenants and agreements of this Lease shall not be altered, modified or amended except in writing signed by Landiord and Tenant."
},
{
  "id": "c106",
  "name": "25.6 Severability",
  "text": "25.6 Severability. Any provision of this Lease which shall prove to be invalid, void or iNegal shall in no way affect, impair or invalidate any other provision hereof and the remaining provisions hereof shall nevertheless remain in full farce and effect."
},
{
  "id": "c107",
  "name": "25.7 Governing Law",
  "text": "25.7 Governing Law. This Lease shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the state in which the Premises are located."
},
{
  "id": "c108",
  "name": "25.8 Notices",
  "text": "25.8 Naftices. All notices to be given by Landlord or Tenant shall be in writing and shall be personally delivered, sent registered or certified mail, postage prepaid, or sent by a nationally recognized courier service that issues a receipt, to the other party af the address in this Section (or fo such other address as may be designated by notice to the other party) and shail be deemed given upon the earfier of personal delivery, the date postmarked, delivery fo such courier or the refusal to accept such service: If to Landlord: Pathmark Stores, Inc. Attn: Senior Vice President of Retail Development 200 Milik Street Carteret, New Jersey 07008 With a copy to: Pathmark Stores, Inc. Attn: Vice President and Real Estate Counsel 200 Milik Street Carteret, New Jersey 07008 if fo Tenant: Gander Mountain Company Attn: Real Estate Department 4567 American Boulevard West Minneapolis, MN 55437 With a capy to: Gander Mountain Company Attn: Legal Department 4567 American Boulevard West Minneapolis, MN 55437"
},
{
  "id": "c109",
  "name": "25.9 Force Majeure",
  "text": "25.9 Force Majeure. Time periods or deadlines for Landlord's performance under any provisions of this Lease shall be extended for periods of time during which performance is prevented due to circumstances beyond the Landlord's control, including, without limitation, labor disputes, embargoes, governmental restrictions or regulations, inclement weather and other acts of God, acts of Tenant, war or other strife, Time periods or deadlines for Tenant's performance under any provisions of this Lease (other than the payment of money) shall be extended for periods of time during which performance is prevented due to circumstances beyond Tenant's control, including, without limitation, labor disputes, embargoes, governmental restrictions or regulations, inclement weather and other acts of God, acts of Landlord, war or other strife. Notwithstanding the foregoing, any extension of time hereunder shall be conditioned upon the party seeking an extension of time delivering written notice of such delay to the other party within ten (10) days of the event causing the delay."
},
{
  "id": "c110",
  "name": "25.10 No Partnership",
  "text": "25.10 No Partnership. Nothing contained in this Lease shall be deemed or construed by the parties hereto or by any third person to create a principal and agent relationship, a partnership, a joint venture, or any other association between Landiord and Tenant."
},
{
  "id": "c111",
  "name": "25.11 Memorandum of Lease",
  "text": "25.11 Memorandum of Lease. The parties agree not to record this Lease. Landlord and Tenant agree to execute, acknowledge and deliver, at the time of execution hereof, a Memorandum of Lease in the form attached as Exhibit G. Tenant may, at its cost, record the Memorandum."
},
{
  "id": "c112",
  "name": "25.12 Consent",
  "text": "25.42 Consent. Exceptas expressly provided otherwise, wherever in this Lease Landlord or Tenant is required to give its consent or approval, such consent or approval shall not be unreasonably withheld, conditioned or delayed."
},
{
  "id": "c113",
  "name": "25.13 Waiver of Landlord's Lien",
  "text": "25.13 Waiver of Landlord's Lien. Landiord hereby waives any contractual, statutory, or other Landlord's lien on Tenant's furniture, fixtures, supplies, equipment and inventory."
},
{
  "id": "c114",
  "name": "25.14 Brokers",
  "text": "25.14 Brokers. Landlord and Tenant represent and warrant to the other that, except for any commission or fee owed to Levin Realty Services, LLC, which amountis to be paid by Landlord by separate agreement, there are no other claims for brokerage commissions or finder's fees in connection with the execution of this Lease and each party agrees to indemnify the other against and hold them harmless from ail liabilities arising from any such claim related to a broker hired by such party."
},
{
  "id": "c115",
  "name": "25.15 Counterparts/Facsimile Copies",
  "text": "25.15 Counterparts/Facsimile Copies. This Lease may be executed in counterparts, all of which taken together shall constitute one and the same instrument. Landlord and Tenant agree that facsimile executed copies of this Lease shall be binding."
},
{
  "id": "c116",
  "name": "25.16 Holding Over",
  "text": "25.16 Holding Over. If Tenant shall retain possession of the Premises after fermination or expiration of this Lease without Landlord's consent, such holding over shall be deemed to constitute a tenancy from month ta month, upon the same terms and conditions as herein provided except that the monthly Base Rent shall be increased to two hundred percent (200%) of the monthly Base Rent in effect immediately prior fo such holdover. in no event shall the tenancy created by such holdover be deemed to be any period longer than month to month."
},
{
  "id": "c117",
  "name": "25.17 Time of the Essence",
  "text": "25.17 Time of the Essence. Time shall be of the essence in interpreting the provisions of this Lease."
},
{
  "id": "c118",
  "name": "25.18 Acceptance",
  "text": "25.18 Acceptance. The offer to lease set forth in this Lease must be accepted by Landlord by the delivery of fully executed facsimile copies hereof (with originals to follow) to Tenant - by April 16, 2004; otherwise, this offer may, at Tenant's sole option, be terminated and be of no further force or effect."
},
{
  "id": "c119",
  "name": "25.19 Lease Provisions",
  "text": "25.19 Lease Provisions. All provisions of this Lease have been negotiated by both parties at arm's length and neither party shall be deemed the scrivener of this Lease. This Lease shail not be construed for or against either party by reason of the authorship or alleged authorship of any provision hereof,"
},
{
  "id": "c120",
  "name": "26. Conditions to Tenant's Obligations",
  "text": "26. CONDITIONS TO TENANT'S OBLIGATIONS. In addition to any other rights of termination in this Lease, Tenant's obligations under this Lease are subject to the satisfaction, in Tenant's sole and absolute discretion, of the following conditions (\"Tenant Conditions\"), and if any of such conditions are nat satisfied on or before the Contingency Date, then Tenant only may, in its sole election, terminate this Lease by written notice to Landiord:"
},
{
  "id": "c121",
  "name": "26.1 Affidavit; Subordination Agreement",
  "text": "26.1 Affidavit: Subordination Agreement. On or before the later of forty-five (45) days following the date of execution of this lease or the Commencement Date (“Contingency Date’), (a) any party holding a mortgage or other similar interest in the Land has executed a Subordination Agreement; and (b) Landlord has executed an owner's or lessor’s affidavit."
},
{
  "id": "c122",
  "name": "26.2 Survey",
  "text": "26.2 Survey. On or before the Contingency Date, Tenant shall be satisfied in its sole discretion with a survey of the Land and the Premises."
},
{
  "id": "c123",
  "name": "26.3 Phase I Environmental Audit",
  "text": "26.3 Phase | Environmental Audit. On or before the Contingency Date, Tenant shall be satisfied in its sole discretion with the environmental condition of the Premises."
},
{
  "id": "c124",
  "name": "26.4 Completion of Documents",
  "text": "26.4 Completion of Documents. On or before the Contingency Date, this Lease and all exhibits hereto shall be completed to the full satisfaction of Tenant, including the completion of all blanks, bracketed references and incomplete exhibits. Upon satisfaction of such, Landlord and Tenant agree to execute a conformed copy of this Lease with all such provided information."
},
{
  "id": "c125",
  "name": "26.5 Access; Parking",
  "text": "26.5 Access: Parking. On or before the Contingency Date, Tenant shall be satisfied with the access to the Premises and the availability of adequate parking for the Premises. Such satisfaction shall require at a minimum, but shall not be limited fo, (a) the conversion of the right-in right-out access from Harry “L” Drive to full access (“Access Conversion’); and (b) demonstration of a parking ratio at least equal to four and two-tenths (4.2) parking spaces for each one thousand (1,000) square feet of Rentable Area of the Premises (after taking into account all exclusions from the Rentable Area of the Premises)."
},
{
  "id": "c126",
  "name": "26.6 No Change",
  "text": "26.6 No Change. On or before the Contingency Date, there has been no material adverse change in the marketability of the Premises, the access to the Premises, the availability of utilities to the Premises, the environmental condition of the Premises or the Premises, the condition of the Building and the Premises or the facts and circumstances satisfying any of the conditions set out herein."
},
{
  "id": "c127",
  "name": "27. Easement or Operation Agreements; Governmental Agreements",
  "text": "2i. EASEMENT OR OPERATION AGREEMENTS: GOVERNMENTAL AGREEMENTS. Landiord agrees that it will not (a) enter into any agreements with respect to the Premises, including without limitation any easement and/or operation agreements and any development, restrictions or other agreement with a governmental authority; or (b) amend any existing such agreements (including without limitation those set forth on Exhibit G), in each case without the prior written consent of Tenant, which consent Tenant may not unreasonably withhold. With respect to all such agreements, Landlord agrees (1} to perform and observe all of the terms, conditions and covenants imposed upon a party thereunder as applicable to the Land and the Premises; (2) to use reasonable efforts and diligence to enforce ail of the provisions thereof against all of the parties thereunder; (3) not to modify or amend any such agreement in any manner without Tenant's prior written consent, which consent Tenant may not unreasonably withhold; and (4) that the Premises shall include the easements and other appurtenant rights derived therefrom and any other any rights or benefits accruing to Landlord with respect fo the Premises."
},
{
  "id": "c128",
  "name": "28. Waiver of Trial by Jury",
  "text": "28. WAIVER OF TRIAL BY JURY. Landlord and Tenant do hereby waive trial by jury in any action, proceeding or counterclaim brought by either against the other upon any matters whatsoever arising oul of or in any way connected with this Lease, Tenant's use or occupancy of the Premises, and/or any claim of injury or damage."
},
{
