    "id": "c135",
    "name": "Declaration §1. Restrictions",
    "text": "Restrictions. For so long as the Premises are used for the Specific Excluded Use (as defined herein), No portion of the Restricted Property may be used by a tenant or occupant for the retail sales and rental of hunting (including without limitation firearms and ammunition), fishing, camping and outdoor apparel, products, equipment and related accessories (and related retail sales and rental of videotapes, cassette tapes, compact discs or any other visual or audio products), retail sales, rental and service of all-terrain vehicles and related sparts vehicles, retail sales and rental of canoes, kayaks and other similar vessels and other uses incidental thereto, to the extent that such sales, in the aggregate, exceed five percent (5%) of its retail sales (“Specific Excluded Use\")."
  },
  {
    "id": "c136",
    "name": "Declaration §2. Termination of Restrictions",
    "text": "2, Termination of Restrictions. The restrictions in Section 1 shall terminate on the expiration or termination of the Gander Mountain Lease."
  },
  {
    "id": "c137",
    "name": "Declaration §3. Benefit and Enforcement",
    "text": "3. Benefit and Enforcement. This Declaration of Restrictions is made for the benefit of and may be enforced by Tenant under the Gander Mountain Lease. Restricted Party acknowledges that damages are not adequate for enforcement of this Declaration of Restrictions, and agrees that it may be enforced by injunction or other appropriate equitable remedies."
  },
  {
    "id": "c138",
    "name": "Declaration §4. Run with the Land",
    "text": "4. Run with the Land. This Declaration of Restrictions shall run with the land and shall bind Restricted Party and its successors and assigns as owners of the Restricted Property. However, each owner of the Restricted Property or any portion thereof shall be liable under this Declaration only with respect to the parcel owned by it, and only during Its period of ownership."
  },
  {
    "id": "c139",
    "name": "SNDA Recital A — Property",
    "text": "A. Landlord owns the property legafly described in Exhibit A attached hereto (“Property”)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c140",
    "name": "SNDA Recital B — Premises and Lease",
    "text": "B. Landlord has leased the Property to Tenant (\"Premises\") pursuant to that certain Lease dated as of April 16, 2004, and all amendments, supplements and additions thereto (\"Lease\")."
  },
  {
    "id": "c141",
    "name": "SNDA Recital C — Mortgage",
    "text": "C. Lender now holds or is about to become the holder of a mortgage which is or will be recorded against the Property (\"Mortgage\")."
  },
  {
    "id": "c142",
    "name": "SNDA Recital D — Subordination and nondisturbance",
    "text": "D. Tenant has agreed to subordinate the Lease to the lien of the Mortgage and Lender has agreed to grant nondisturbance righis to Tenant, on the terms and conditions hereinafter set forth."
  },
  {
    "id": "c143",
    "name": "SNDA §1. Subordination",
    "text": "1. Subordination. Tenant agrees that the Lease and all of the terms, covenants and provisions thereof are, and shall al aif times continue to be, subordinate in all respects to the lien of the Mortgage and to all renewals, modifications, supplements, replacements and extensions thereof with the same force and effect as if the Mortgage had been executed, delivered and recorded prior to the execution and delivery of the Lease."
  },
  {
    "id": "c144",
    "name": "SNDA §2. Nondisturbance",
    "text": "2. Nondisturbance. So long as neither the Lease nor Tenant's right of possession of the Premises pursuant thereto shall have been terminated by reason of a default by Tenant under the Lease (beyond any period provided Tenant in the Lease fo cure such default), Lender agrees that Tenant's possession of the Property and Tenant's other rights and privileges under the Lease or any extensions or renewals thereof, shall not be diminished, disturbed or interfered with by Lender and if any action or proceeding is commenced by Lender for the foreclosure of the Mortgage and/or the sale of the Property, Tenant shall not be named as a party defendant therein unless required by law but only provided the terms of this Section are complied with. Should Lender become the owner of the Property, or should the Property be sold by reason of foreclosure, or other proceedings brought to enforce the Mortgage, or should the Property be transferred by deed in tieu of foreclosure, or should any portion of the Property be sold under a trustee's sale, the Lease will continue in full force and effect as a direct lease between the Lender and/or the succeeding owner of the Premises, as he case may be, and the Tenant, upon and subject to all of the ferms, covenants and conditions of the Lease for the balance of its term as it may be extended, and Lender, or any successor owner of the Premises, will be bound by all of the terms of the Lease, Lender agrees that so jong as the Lease ts in full force and effect, no proper exercise by Tenant of its rights under the Lease shall constitute a default under the Mortgage or require Lender's consent, and that any conflict between the terms of the Lease and the terms of the Mortgage shall be resolved in favor of the Lease."
  },
  {
    "id": "c145",
    "name": "SNDA §3. Attornment — proceedings",
    "text": "3. Attornment. Tenant agrees that the institution of any action or other proceedings by Lender under the Mortgage in order to realize upon Landlord's interest in the Property shall not result in the cancellation or termination of the Lease or Tenant's obligations thereunder."
  },
  {
    "id": "c146",
    "name": "SNDA §3(a). Lease unaffected",
    "text": "(a) the Lease shall not be terminated or affected thereby;"
  },
  {
    "id": "c147",
    "name": "SNDA §3(b). Attornment to Lender",
    "text": "(b} Tenant shail attorn to Lender and recognize Lender as its fandiord under the Lease for the unexpired term of the Lease, subject to all of the terms and conditians of the Lease and such attornment shall be effective and self-operative without the execution of any further instrument on the part of Lender or Tenant;"
  },
  {
    "id": "c148",
    "name": "SNDA §3(c). New lease",
    "text": "(c) if, by operation of law, or otherwise, the commencement of any action or other proceedings by Lender under the Mortgage or the entry into and taking possession of the Premises shall result in the cancellation or termination of the Lease or Tenant's obligations thereunder, Tenant shall, upon request, execute and deliver a new lease of the Premises containing the same terms and conditions as contained in the Lease (Including all right of renewal and extension), for the remaining term thereof, and (d)"
  },
  {
    "id": "c149",
    "name": "SNDA §3(d). Lender limitations",
    "text": "(d) Lender shall not be: (i) responsible or liable for any monetary damages as a result of, or obligated to cure, any defaults by Landlord under the Lease provided ihat the foregoing shal! not be deemed to relieye Lender or any other party from the obligation to perform any obligation of the Landlord under the Lease which remains unperformed at the time that Lender or any other party succeeds to the interest of Landlord under the Lease; (il) subject to claims, defenses or offsets under the Lease or against Landlord which arose or existed prior to the time Lender obtains possession of the Property provided that the foregoing shall not be deemed to (A) relieve Lender or any other party from the obligation to perform any obligation of the Landlord under the Lease which remains unperformed at the time that Lender or any other party succeeds to the interest of Landlord under the Lease, or (B) modify or waive any rights of self-help, set-off, abatement or termination expressly provided in the Lease; (iii) bound by any rent paid more than thirty (30) days in advance; {iv} liable for the return of any security deposit paid to any prior fandiord, including Landlord, unless Lender has actually received the same; or (v) bound by any amendment or modification of the Lease made without its prior written consent (Lender agrees not to unreasonably withhold or delay its consent to any proposed amendment or modification which does not materially and adversely affect Lender's security). Nothing in this Section shail be deemed a waiver of any rights or remedies that Tenant may possess or claim personally against Landlord for any defaults or acts of Landiord."
  },
  {
    "id": "c150",
    "name": "SNDA §4. Right To Cure Landlord's Default",
    "text": "4. Right To Cure Landiord’s Default. Notwithstanding any provisions of the Lease to the contrary, no notice of cancellation of the Lease by Tenant shall be effective unless Lender shall have first received notice of the default giving rise to such cancellation and shail have failed, for a period of thirty (30) days after receipt thereof, to cure such default. Tenant will forward to Lender coples of any statement, notice, claim or demand given or made by Tenant to Landlord, in all cases by the same method as the statement, notice, claim or demand was given or made to Landlord."
  },
  {
    "id": "c151",
    "name": "SNDA §5. Assignment of Lease",
    "text": "5. Assignment of Lease. Tenant acknowledges that Landlord is assigning the Lease and rents thereunder to Lender as security for the note given by Landlord to Lender. Tenant agrees that upon receipt of a written notice from Lender, it wilt thereafter pay to Lender directly all rent and other amounts due or to become due from time to time under the Lease. Lender acknowledges it agrees that Tenant shall have the right to rely upon any such notice from Lender and that Tenant may pay such rents and other amounts to Lender without any obligation or right to determine the actual existence of the right of Lender to receive such rents and other amounts, notwithstanding any notice from or claim of Landlord to the contrary. Landlord shall have no right or claim against Tenant for any such rents and other amounts so paid by Tenant to Lender and Landlord waives and releases any such claims. Landlord and Lender agree that Tenant shall be credited under the Lease for any payments sent to Lender pursuant to such written notice. in addition, Lender agrees to indemnify and hold harmless Tenant from and against any and all claims by Landlord in any way related to Tenant's compliance with this Section."
  },
  {
    "id": "c152",
    "name": "SNDA §6. Casualty and Condemnation",
    "text": "6. Casualty and Gondemnation. Lender agrees that so long as neither the Lease nor Tenant's right of possession of the Property shall have been terminated by reason of a default by Tenant under the Lease (beyond any period provided Tenant ts in the Lease to cure such default), if the Premises shall be damaged or destroyed by fire or other casualty, or taken by condemnation, then notwithstanding any contrary provision contained in the Mortgage, Lender will make the proceeds of insurance, or condemnation award, available for the purpose of repairing and restoring the Premises, as the case may be, in accordance with the terms of the Lease and subject to such reasonable and customary procedures with respect to the disbursement thereof as Lender may impose."
  },
  {
    "id": "c153",
    "name": "SNDA §7. Notices",
    "text": "7. Notices. All notices or other communications required or permitted to be given by this Agreement shall be in writing and shall be personally delivered, sent registered or certified mail, postage prepaid, or sent by a nationally recognized courier service that issues a receipt, to the other party at the address in this Section (or to such other address as may be designated by notice to the other party) and shall be deemed given upon the earlier of personal delivery, the date postmarked, delivery to such courier or the refusal to accept such service: Lender: Attn: Tenant: Gander Mountain Company Altn: Real Estate Department 4567 American Boulevard West Minneapolis, MN 55437 With a copy fo: Gander Mountain Company Atin: Legal Department 4567 American Boulevard West Minneapolis, MN 55437 if to Landlord: Pathmark Stores, inc. Altn: Senior Vice President of Retait Development 200 Milik Street Carteret, New Jersey 07008 With @ copy to: Pathmark Stores, Inc. Alin: Vice President and Real Estate Counsel 200 Milik Street Carteret, New Jersey 07008"
  },
  {
    "id": "c154",
    "name": "SNDA §8. Successors and Assigns",
    "text": "8. Successors and Assigns. This Agreement shail be binding upon and inure fo the benefit of the respective heirs, personal representatives, successors and assigns of Lender, Tenant and Landlord and any person or entity that takes title to the Property by virtue of a foreclosure sale or otherwise. This Agreement shall not modify or in any way affect Landlord's obligations under the Lease."
  },
  {
    "id": "c155",
    "name": "SNDA §9. Amendment",
    "text": "9. ‘Amendment. This Agreement may be amended only bya written agreement signed. by Lender, Landlord and Tenant."
  },
  {
    "id": "c156",
    "name": "SNDA §10. Governing Law",
    "text": "10. Governing Law. This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the state where the Property is located."
  },
  {
    "id": "c157",
    "name": "SNDA §11. Counterparts",
    "text": "44. Counterparts. This Agreement may be executed in counterparts, all of which taken together shall constitute one and the same instrument and any of the parties hereto may execute this Agreement by signing any such counterpart. Lender and Tenant agree thal facsimile executed copies of this Agreement shall be binding. Original copies of this Agreement shall be circulated and signed by Tenant and Lender as soon as practicable after closing of the loan."
  },
  {
    "id": "c158",
    "name": "SNDA §12. Tenant Financing",
    "text": "12. Tenant Financing. Tenant shall have the absolute right from fime to time during the term of the Lease and without Landlord's or Lender's further approval written or otherwise, (o collaterally assign or to grant and assign a mortgage or other security interest in Tenant's interest in the Lease and all of Tenani's property to Tenant's lenders in connection with Tenant's financing arrangements. Lender agrees to execute such confirmation certificates and other documents as Tenant's lenders may reasonably request in connection with any such financing provided the same are in a form acceptable to Lender."
  },
  {
    "id": "c159",
    "name": "SNDA §13. Entire Agreement",
    "text": "13. Entire Agreement. This Agreement contains the entire agreement between the parlies respecting the subject matter contained herein and supersedes all prior or contemporaneous written or oral agreements and negotiations between the parties."
  },
